DESCRIPTION:Explore and enjoy music and dance from around the world!\nCele
 brate the rhythms\, cultures\, and global creativity that make our communi
 ty shine at the\nOccidental World Music & Dance Festival\n! This joyful\, 
 immersive event brings together extraordinary musicians and dancers from a
 round the world for a day filled with exhilarating performances\, interact
 ive workshops\, and irresistible rhythms. From captivating traditional art
 istry to innovative contemporary fusion\, the festival invites audiences o
 f all ages to experience the beauty of global cultures up close. With food
 \, vendors\, community activities\, and plenty of space to dance\, it’s 
 a feast for the senses and a celebration of unity through music and moveme
 nt. Come be part of one of Occidental’s most beloved and uplifting tradi
 tions!\nGet tickets\nTicket prices\n$75 through May 29\n$80 at the door\nK
 ids 12 and under free\, Half price for teens\nA limited number of scholars
 hips is available.\nClick here to apply for a scholarship to the event.\nM
 ore Than 50 sessions to choose from!\nEnjoy a variety of performances\, wo
 rkshops\, jams\, drum circles and demonstrations\nplus:\nMusical Instrumen
 t Lending Library\nCeltic Harp Encounter\nArt Gallery\nFree instrument che
 ck • Free parking\nLata’s Indian Cuisine Lunch\nMediterranean Dinner\n
 Scroll down to see the list of presenters..\nOur preliminary schedule is n
 ow available! Click here to view the schedule.\nSponsored by:\nLoveland Vi
 olin Shop\nLiving History Centre\nSOLFUL\nInterested in sponsorship? Pleas
 e contact us!\nKhatch Khatchadourian\nDodona\nPERFORMANCES\nKhatchadour Kh
 atchadourian - Armenian Music\nDodona - Music of Greece & Albania\nThunder
  Clappers Native American Dancers\nSol Flamenco\nJenny Kerr & Friends - So
 uthern Delta Blues\nStory Wrens\nWill Marsh - Sitar music of India\nJoss J
 affe - Tabla\, West African N’goni\nLos Bahianatos\nGradina - Balkan Mus
 ic\nMeredith Axelrod and Craig Ventresco - Ragtime & Vintage Jazz\nCarey D
 ubbert and Meredith Axelrod - Autoharp\nKatiana Vilá - Iberian Songs\nLos
  Bahianatos - Colombian Cumbia & Vallenato\nMichael Hubbert - Uilleann Bag
 pipes\nRaman Osman - Kurdish Music\nJanessa Lynna - Belly Dance\nStory Wre
 ns - Story Songs of the British Isles\nBobby Edwards - Swiss Alpenhorn\nKe
 n Genetti - Zithers from Around the World\nScroll down to see the workshop
 s\n2026 Workshops & Demos\nClick here to see workshop leaders' bios\nSlow 
 Tunes and French Jam - Jason Adajian\nIrish Songs - Shay Black\, Hector Br
 agado\nIrish Fiddle - Paul Chaffee\nIrish Dance - Shay Black\, Hector Brag
 ado\, Paul Chaffee\nWake Up Your Voice: A Global Singalong - Maria Culbers
 on\nBalkan Singing - Darina Drapkin\nBalkan Drumming - Sean Tergis\nBalkan
  Dancing - Sue Williard\nBrazilian Guitar - Ian Faquini\nFlamenco Dance - 
 Joelle Goncalves\nOld Timey Jam - Michael Greenberg\nCuban & Puerto Rican 
 Songs - Michael & Leslie Hubbert\nJazz Beyond Borders - Greg Johnson\nBlue
 s Harmonica - Jenny Kerr\nWest African Dance - Tyehimba Kokayi\nWest Afric
 an Drumming - Lion’s Den Institute\nBelly Dance - Janessa Lynna\nCuban &
  Latin Drumming - Carlitos Medrano\nAmp Care & Repair - Philbillie Milner\
 nGentle Yoga - Pauline Persichili\nSong Circle - Celia Ramsay\nColombian C
 umbia and Vallenato - Chris Reid & Friends\nEasy Irish Tunes - Mark Sellin
 \nNative American Flute & Meditation - Al Striplen\nWomen’s Songs of Res
 istance - Holly Tannen\nFlamenco Guitar - Mark Taylor\nRed Hot (guitar) St
 rings - Craig Ventresco\nIndian Rhythms & Bols - Joss Jaffe\nArabic Drummi
 ng - Faisal Zedan\nUnlocking Your Voice: Friendly\nMasterclass - Sophia Zi
 mmerman
