BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Morning Yoga
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260608T100000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260608T111000
UID:69cdcb76231e9843a01a106b@squarespace.com
DESCRIPTION:Regenerative Ayurvedic Yoga with Tirza Dawn\nCome\, step onto 
 your mat with an open heart and an open mind.\nInvest in your self care an
 d join us for morning yoga in the OCA studio. $20 per class\, $15 for OCA 
 members. Yoga is offered Mondays from 10-11:10 AM and also on Wednesdays f
 rom 8:30-9:40 AM. The registration below is for Mondays.\nPay at the door 
 for a-la-carte sessions or use the links below to pay ahead for four weeks
  at a time.\nPay Online 4 sessions - OCA members\nPay Online 4 sessions - 
 non members\nTirza Dawn Naramore\nis a yogi\, mother\, artist\, ceremonial
 ist and lover of life. She has been practicing and teaching yoga and medit
 ation for 30 years and offers yoga retreats and trainings that center on o
 ptimum health\, self realization and self love. Her teachers are from many
  yoga and tantric traditions\, but her primary lineages are Iyengar and Ka
 li Ray.\nTirza is deeply devoted to community building and is honored to h
 ave created a number of community supported non profits including Mystic F
 amily Circus and The AWAKEN Project\, which serves families with children 
 on the autism spectrum. Tirza is proud to be the mother of 3 wild teenager
 s\, including her incredible son who is diagnosed with autism.\nTirza’s 
 spirituality is one of many influences and teachings. Beginning with a Chr
 istian up-bringing and being raised on a Christian commune in her early ch
 ildhood\, she later expanded into more earth-based ways. While in her 20
 ’s Tirza was adopted into the Native American Church\, where she learned
  from her relatives a way of living the “Beauty Way.”\nDuring the 1990
 ’s and early 2000’s\, Tirza lived in San Francisco\, Oakland and Berke
 ley\, directing the Mystic Family Circus\, which was a performance group d
 edicated to cultural awareness and bridge building. She worked with Cirque
  du Soleil\, Burning Man\, Reclaiming\, Contraband\, CELLspace and other B
 ay Area art collectives and non profits to provide conscious entertainment
  and “prayerformances” for the betterment of humankind and the planet.
 \nIn 2012\, Tirza helped to found the Buckeye Gathering\, an ancestral ski
 lls gathering in Northern California which draws teachers and students of 
 all ages to learn ancestral ways of tending the earth and survival skills.
 \nTirza Dawn was the founder of yoga programming and the Ayurvedic Yoga Te
 acher Trainings at the dhyana Center of Ayurveda in Sebastopol\, Californi
 a\, which operated a community center of healing and education from 2010 t
 o 2020.
LOCATION:Occidental Center for the Arts Studio\, 3820 Doris Murphy Court\,
  Occidental CA 95465
URL:https://www.occidentalcenterforthearts.org/upcoming-events/ew6dc3w3s87
 emgn-f7ghs-2rk62-tnnpx-6xmnb-lsdsy-cgk36-68rbe-wfhyw-sajgf-g5mrg-59cpa
X-SOURCE:Occidental Center for the Arts
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Sound Bath with guest practitioners Siren Sisters
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260609T190000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260609T203000
UID:69ade30af944ed0aba13295d@squarespace.com
DESCRIPTION:Rest & Renew at our Sound Bath!\nSupport your nervous system\,
  release anxiety and stress\, and harmonize your body\, mind and spirit on
  the 2nd Tuesday of every month!\nJune 9th's sound bath will be hosted by 
 special guests Siren Sisters Sound.\nSiren Sisters Sound is a sound healin
 g duo created by Allyson Hallett and Allie Evans\, rooted in a shared love
  for music\, connection\, and holistic healing. Through the use of crystal
  and metal singing bowls\, chimes\, flutes\, drums\, and vocal channeling\
 , they create immersive sound experiences that promote deep relaxation\, e
 motional release\, and nervous system restoration. As certified sound heal
 ers and Reiki practitioners\, they intentionally curate spaces that suppor
 t grounding\, reflection\, and inner balance.\nWe hope you'll join for thi
 s unique experience in the OCA Studio. Laura Benson will be back in July f
 or her usual monthly sound healing on the 14th.\nBring your own yoga mat &
  blanket and come ready to rest and renew! In the OCA Studio.\nSliding sca
 le pricing $25-$35.\nRegister\nA sound bath is a whole-body\, immersive li
 stening experience. During a sound bath\, participants often sit or lie do
 wn\, and are surrounded by the mostly non-melodic soundscapes created by a
  range of instruments played by the sound bath facilitator. Hence\, they a
 re “bathed” in sound.\nSound therapy is a non-invasive healing modalit
 y that utilizes the physical and physiological interactions of sound on ou
 r bodies and nervous systems to produce therapeutic results. In a sound he
 aling session\, specific sonic frequencies are used to soothe the central 
 nervous system\, calm the breath\, and quiet the mind by encouraging the b
 rain to move into more relaxed states\, down from beta (fight-or-flight) a
 nd into theta and alpha waves. This increases present-moment awareness and
  reduces stress and anxiety. Sound baths have been found to be effective i
 n improving mood\, cognitive function\, and overall mental\, physical\, an
 d spiritual wellbeing.\nCrystal bowl sound baths are particularly powerful
  in that each bowl is tuned to a specific frequency that corresponds with 
 a different chakra\, or energy center\, of the body. Based on specific nee
 ds\, a practitioner can focus on releasing tension or clearing out stuck e
 nergy in specific chakras by playing certain bowls or intervals.\nWhile at
 tending a sound bath\, you may experience physical sensations brought out 
 by the crystal sound bowls or gong\, such as tingling in your limbs or sca
 lp\, slowing of your breathing\, eye flutters\, or small muscle spasms. No
 t to worry! These sensations often indicate the release of tension or emot
 ional energy stored in the body’s energy systems.
LOCATION:Occidental Center for the Arts\, 3850 Doris Murphy Court\, Occide
 ntal\, CA 95465
URL:https://www.occidentalcenterforthearts.org/upcoming-events/rest-renew-
 monthly-sound-bath-l5n5c-wchlw-38gmc-rw262-hd6w3-nlnhm-bn8b8-d74pg-d79je-w
 x3an-ampe7-zckp7-gndtj-32c6f-4y8an-wsmxr-y3rtb-8k62p
X-SOURCE:Occidental Center for the Arts
END:VEVENT
